you're going to hate it?

318
01:32:16,760 --> 01:32:17,880
No, your parents give you things

319
01:32:17,880 --> 01:32:20,320
they think that you're going to like, hopefully.

320
01:32:20,320 --> 01:32:21,200
They're nice parents, anyway.

321
01:32:21,200 --> 01:32:23,080
They give you stuff they think that you're going to like.

322
01:32:23,080 --> 01:32:25,080
So the very fact that they're giving it to you,

323
01:32:25,080 --> 01:32:26,720
that may provide some information.

324
01:32:26,720 --> 01:32:27,720
Look, they're going and saying,

325
01:32:27,720 --> 01:32:29,920
look, this is your special bicycle.

326
01:32:29,920 --> 01:32:30,920
Right, and we picked it out.

327
01:32:30,920 --> 01:32:32,440
We think this is one that you're really going to like.

328
01:32:32,440 --> 01:32:34,280
It's just the right, right for you.

329
01:32:34,280 --> 01:32:36,000
We thought about it, really enjoyed it.

330
01:32:36,000 --> 01:32:37,920
Or sometimes you may say, look, this is a book

331
01:32:37,920 --> 01:32:39,400
that I loved when I was your age,

332
01:32:39,400 --> 01:32:41,200
and I think you might like it, too.

333
01:32:41,200 --> 01:32:44,480
Right, so here, there's information being given,

334
01:32:44,480 --> 01:32:46,800
and the fact that it's your endowment

335
01:32:46,800 --> 01:32:49,080
actually might tell you something in the real world.

336
01:32:49,080 --> 01:32:51,960
Right, or the status quo in a restaurant.

337
01:32:51,960 --> 01:32:53,560
Do restaurants randomly decide

338
01:32:53,560 --> 01:32:55,160
what the contents of a Big Mac will be?

339
01:32:55,160 --> 01:32:57,080
Like McDonald's say, well, let's see, what is this?

